    {
      "id": 151,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -790,
        5080
      ],
      "size": [
        900,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MiniMax H3 - ~40 s PREVIEW at full quality: 640x384, 22 frames (~0.9 s), all 8 steps, exact attention, H3-Turbo Fast UNET Loader\n\nMeasured on this RTX 3050 6GB inside ComfyUI (seed change only, same prompt, everything already loaded):\n  text encode   cached (0 s)\n  sampler       ~24 s   (8 x 2.8 s; measured 2.78 s/step, plus ~1 s to rebuild the engine after the VAE)\n  VAE decode    14 s + audio 1.4 s + save 0.7 s\n  total         ~40 s   (measured 48.1 s BEFORE the pinned-staging fix, which removes ~8 s: restart ComfyUI once to load it)\n\nWhat costs more than 40 s, and why:\n  - First run after starting ComfyUI: ~3 min (text encoder 65 s + model 79 s read from the D: drive).\n  - NEW prompt: +15-65 s for the text encoder (Qwen3-VL 32B), even when warm.\n  - Longer or bigger clips: the model attends over every token, so cost grows faster than length:\n      832x480 x 124 frames (5 s)  ~6.5 min sampler (measured)     512x320 x 481 frames (20 s) ~14 min sampler (measured)\n  - 608x352 x 22 frames is ~3-4 s faster than this preset.\nattention = int8_fast on the loader is faster on long clips but is a different sample (not bit-identical to UNETLoader).\n\nNeeds the H3-Turbo custom node and the converted model in models/h3turbo/ (h3turbo h3-convert ...). No run-time LoRAs on this loader.\nModels: clip/qwen3vl-32B-MiniMax-H3-Q2_K.gguf (ComfyUI-GGUF), vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors + vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors"
      ]
    }
  ],
